  "title": "Thomas Mann Archive Extended Opening Times And Change In Location",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Main article",
      "text": "From Monday 11 July, the archive, library and Thomas Mann’s last study will be accessible at the new location with extended opening times: Monday to Friday from 10.00 to 17.00.\n\nThe provisional location is on the Hönggerberg Campus :\n\nHCP Building/G Level Room no. 21.2 – 24.2 Leopold-Ruzicka-Weg 4 8093 Zurich\n\nYou can reach Hönggerberg in 15 minutes from Zentrum with the convenient ETH-Link, ETH Zurich’s shuttlebus between the two campuses .\n\nOnce the building has been fully renovated, the University of Zurich will find a new purpose for the Bodmer-Haus, where the Thomas Mann Archive was housed from 1961. The Thomas Mann Archive is scheduled to move to a new, permanent site in ETH Zurich’s main building in the medium term."
    }
  ],
